@meta {
    title: Binding regressions
    sdoc-version: 0.2
}

# Binding Regressions @regressions
{
    Every construct in this file was read wrongly by a hand-written Python
    parser that this binding replaced. They are collected here so a regression
    names the shape it broke rather than "a document stopped parsing".

    # Short Row @short-row {
        A row may carry fewer cells than the header. The grammar states no
        cell-count rule, so neither does the reader. The old parser raised
        here, and rejected three real documents for it.

        {[table]
            Property | Where | Note
            Contiguous | spans.py | it is
            Short row | only two cells
        }
    }

    # Column Directive Row @directive-row {
        The alignment row is a directive, not data. The reference removes it
        from `rows`, so row-to-line attribution must remove the same line — a
        half-fix puts every later citation one row out and looks right.

        {[table]
            Quantity | Value
            < | >.3
            0 | 0
            0.5 | 1.303713
        }
    }

    # Brace On The Next Line @next-line-brace
    {
        `# Title @anchor` then `{` is the same section as `# Title @anchor {`.
        The old parser required the brace on the heading line and so lost whole
        sections silently — 151 anchored sections across 6 documents, measured
        once before it was deleted. The tables inside a lost section came back
        attributed to no section at all.

        # Nested @next-line-nested
        {
            {[table]
                Field | Type
                tensor | float
            }
        }
    }

    # Unanchored Scopes @transparent {
        An unanchored scope is not an address, so it cannot own a table: the
        table below belongs to @transparent. The heading is still visible as a
        heading, which is how a caller tells this table from one in a sibling
        subsection.

        # Modifiable Parameters {
            {[table]
                Parameter | Default
                threshold | 4
            }
        }
    }

    # Scope Type Annotations @typed {
        A `:type` annotation is not part of the title.

        # Overlap With Homopolymer Rule :warning {
            The heading above is titled "Overlap With Homopolymer Rule".
        }
    }

    # Escaped Pipes @escaped-pipes {
        `\|` is cell content, and arrives unescaped.

        {[table]
            Sequence | Working
            `AGTC` | \|2-2\| - 0 = 0
        }
    }

    # Headerless Tables @headerless {
        `{[table headerless]` has no header, so no body line is one. Getting
        the offset wrong here shifts every cited line by one and drops the last
        row.

        {[table headerless borderless]
            a | b
            c | d
        }
    }

    # Inline Markers @markers {
        All seven sigils, not the four the old reader happened to know.
        `{^note^}`, `{=neutral=}` and `{~highlight~}` survived into "plain
        text" verbatim, in 32 tables across 13 documents.

        {[table]
            Sigil | Written | Status
            positive | plus | {+good+}
            neutral | equals | {=estimated=}
            note | caret | {^weak^}
            caution | question | {?Dormant: pending a ruling?}
            warning | bang | {!fires late!}
            negative | minus | {-bad-}
            highlight | tilde | {~look here~}
        }
    }
}
